= Apache OpenNLP 3.0.0 released
Apache OpenNLP
2026-11-12
:jbake-type: post
:jbake-tags: community
:jbake-status: published
:category: news
:idprefix:

The Apache OpenNLP team is pleased to announce the release of Apache OpenNLP 3.0.0.

The Apache OpenNLP library is a machine learning based toolkit for the processing of natural language text.

It supports the most common NLP tasks, such as tokenization, sentence segmentation, part-of-speech tagging, named entity extraction, chunking, parsing, and coreference resolution.

Apache OpenNLP 3.0.0 binary and source distributions are available for download from our link:/download.html[download page].

The OpenNLP library is distributed by Maven Central as well. See the link:/maven-dependency.html[Maven dependency] page for more details.

== What's new in Apache OpenNLP 3.0.0

Apache OpenNLP 3.0.0 is the *first release of the 3.x line*. It requires Java 21 and splits the toolkit into separate Maven modules;
`opennlp-tools` remains available as an aggregate of the core modules. The migration notes below describe what changes for users of 2.x.

=== Highlights

Compared with 2.x, OpenNLP 3.0.0 brings:

* *Modular artifacts*: `opennlp-api`, `opennlp-runtime`, `opennlp-formats`, `opennlp-cli`, the `opennlp-ml-*` trainers, `opennlp-model-resolver`, `opennlp-spellcheck` and the extension modules.
* *Thread-safe core components*: `POSTaggerME`, `TokenizerME`, `SentenceDetectorME`, `ChunkerME`, `LemmatizerME` and `NameFinderME` can be shared across threads.
* *Unicode text processing*: a normalization engine with offset alignment, full case folding, emoji and emoticon handling, confusable skeletons and a UAX 29 word tokenizer, based on Unicode 18.0 data.
* *Subword tokenization*: Byte Pair Encoding, a WordPiece encoder, SentencePiece inference with spans on the original text, and WordPiece vocabularies from Hugging Face `tokenizer.json` files.
* *Dependency parsing*: a transition-based parser and a feedforward neural parser, both with command-line tools.
* *New components*: SymSpell spell correction, a sentiment detector, SVM document categorization, Hunspell-based stemming and analysis, dictionary-based tokenization for Japanese, Korean and Chinese, and stopword lists.
* *Deep learning*: text embeddings through a provider SPI, GPU inference and batched `embedAll` with padding strategies for `SentenceVectorsDL`, and thread-safe ONNX components.
* *No regular expressions in production code*, enforced at build time, with `CompatibilityMode` and `WhitespaceMode` to reproduce the 2.x output.
* *Security*: a documented link:/security.html[security model], hardened XML parsing and model deserialization, and checksum verification of downloaded models.

=== Migration from 2.x

* Java 21 or later is required.
* `opennlp-tools` still works as a single dependency. For a smaller footprint, depend on `opennlp-runtime` and add the modules you use, for example `opennlp-ml-maxent`, `opennlp-formats` or `opennlp-model-resolver`.
* Renamed artifacts: `opennlp-tools-models` is now `opennlp-model-resolver`, and `opennlp-morfologik-addon` is now `opennlp-morfologik`. Java package names are unchanged.
* Models trained with 1.x or 2.x may depend on the earlier text processing. Until they are retrained, start the JVM with `-Dopennlp.whitespace.mode=LEGACY` and `-Dopennlp.compat.mode=LEGACY`. Both modes are process-wide and must match the mode the models were trained under.
* Public methods of `opennlp-api`, `opennlp-runtime` and `opennlp-spellcheck` throw `IllegalArgumentException` instead of `NullPointerException` for `null` or invalid arguments (GH-1395, GH-1396, GH-1397).
* The core `+*ME+` classes can be shared across threads. The `+ThreadSafe*ME+` wrappers are deprecated.
* Tokenizer: the alphanumeric optimization is configured with a `TokenizerCharacterPolicy`. The `Pattern` variants of the `TokenizerFactory` constructor, `TokenizerFactory.create`, the `TokSpanEventStream` constructor, `TokenizerFactory.getAlphaNumericPattern()`, `Factory.getAlphanumeric(String)` and `Factory.DEFAULT_ALPHANUMERIC` are deprecated for removal in 4.0.
A call that passes `null` as the pattern no longer compiles; use the overloads without that argument, for example `TokenizerFactory.create(null, "eng", null, true)`.
Subclasses that override or call the protected `TokenizerFactory.init` must pass a `TokenizerCharacterPolicy`. Models with a custom `alphaNumericPattern` still load; an invalid pattern now fails with `InvalidFormatException` (GH-1479).
* `BasicContextGenerator(String)` takes the separator literally instead of as a regular expression, rejects a separator containing a backslash, no longer returns empty predicates, and splits on Unicode whitespace by default (OPENNLP-1929).
* `ParserFactory.create` and the chunking and tree insert `Parser` constructors reject a beam size below 1 or an advance percentage outside (0, 1] with `IllegalArgumentException` (GH-1476).
* `AbstractClassPathModelFinder`: the protected `asRegex` and `matchesPattern` methods were removed; use `matchesWildcard(url, "*.bin")` (OPENNLP-1932). `findModels` returns an unmodifiable set (GH-1506).
* `PlainTextByLineStream.reset()` closes the previous reader, so its `InputStreamFactory` must return a new stream for each pass.
* `RealBasicEventStream` reads a line that contains only an outcome as an event without contexts instead of ending the stream.
* AD reader: self-closing markup such as `<s/>` no longer opens a sentence, paragraph, title, box or text, and tag names must match exactly (GH-1447).
* MASC reader: region offsets must consist of ASCII digits without a sign; other documents are skipped (OPENNLP-1990).
* CoNLL-U reader: a multiword token range whose word lines are missing throws `InvalidFormatException` (OPENNLP-1952).
* `EmojiEntityType` gains `HAND`, `SKY_AND_WEATHER` and `TOOL`, and confusable skeletons follow UTS 39 18.0.0 (GH-1347).
* Sentence vectors: GPU sessions use `LONGEST` padding by default for models with token output and a padding token. Set `PaddingStrategy.EXACT_LENGTH` in `SentenceVectorsOptions` to keep unpadded batches (GH-1392). Stored vectors from 2.x should be recomputed.

=== Dependency Updates
* Apache Parent POM 40
* Apache Commons Secure XML 1.1.0 (new)
* Apache UIMA uimaj 3.7.0
* ClassGraph 5.0.2
* ONNX Runtime 1.31.1
* SLF4J 2.0.20
* Maven 3.10.0 via the Maven Wrapper

